  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Finance - additional contribution to United Nations Environment Programme for climate action 2021-2022-2023-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) is the leading UN body on environmental issues and plays a central role in supporting the implementation of the Paris Agreement. UNEP combines scientific assessment, policy support, technical assistance, and climate finance to help countries transition towards low-carbon, climate-resilient development pathways. It is also a key actor in the production of global climate knowledge, including flagship reports such as the Emissions Gap Report and the Adaptation Gap Report, which inform international climate policy and negotiations. [unep.org], [unep.org]
UNEP&#x2019;s climate work is structured around both mitigation and adaptation. On mitigation, UNEP supports countries in reducing greenhouse gas emissions through measures such as renewable energy deployment, energy efficiency, circular economy approaches, and low-carbon development strategies. On adaptation, UNEP helps countries strengthen resilience to climate impacts through nature-based solutions, ecosystem restoration, climate information services, and improved disaster preparedness. UNEP also works to mobilize climate finance and facilitate access to climate technologies, particularly for developing countries. [unep.org], [unep.org]
A distinctive feature of UNEP&#x2019;s climate portfolio is its support for the enabling framework of the Paris Agreement. UNEP assists countries in developing and implementing their Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs), strengthening climate transparency systems, and improving the monitoring and reporting of climate action. Through partnerships such as the UNEP Copenhagen Climate Centre and collaboration with governments, development banks, the private sector, and civil society, UNEP contributes to enhancing countries&#x2019; capacities to meet their adaptation and mitigation commitments while advancing sustainable development objectives.</narrative>
  </description>
